@@ -3212,6 +3212,7 @@ Subtitles
       and the margin of the background box is determined by ``--sub-shadow-offset``.
       The behavior of the outline is the same as the ``outline-and-shadow`` style.
       This corresponds to ``BorderStyle=4``, which is a libass-specific extension.
+      ``--sub-back-radius`` rounds its corners.
 
     Default: ``outline-and-shadow``.
 
@@ -3225,6 +3226,17 @@ Subtitles
           including stats and console
         - ``--profile=box`` applies the ``background-box`` style to both subtitles and OSD
 
+``--sub-back-radius=<size>``
+    Corner radius of the box drawn by ``--sub-border-style=background-box``,
+    in scaled pixels (see ``--sub-font-size`` for details), like
+    ``--sub-shadow-offset``, which sets the margin of the box. The corners
+    are anti-aliased, and the radius is limited to half the box height.
+
+    Like ``--sub-line-spacing``, it does not apply to ASS subtitles with
+    ``--sub-ass-override=no``.
+
+    Default: 0 (square corners).
+
 ``--sub-color=<color>``
     Specify the color used for unstyled text subtitles.
 
